### Step 1: Determine current distribution

The square loop ABCD has two parallel paths for current I: ABC and ADC. The resistance of path ABC is \(R_{ABC} = r\) and the resistance of path ADC is \(R_{ADC} = 2r\). Since the potential difference across parallel paths is the same, we have:
i_1 R_{ABC} = i_2 R_{ADC}
i_1 r = i_2 (2r) \implies i_1 = 2i_2
The total current entering at A is \(I = i_1 + i_2\).
I = 2i_2 + i_2 = 3i_2 \implies i_2 = \frac{I}{3}
i_1 = 2i_2 = \frac{2I}{3}

### Step 2: Calculate magnetic field due to each segment

The magnetic field at the center of a square loop due to a straight wire segment is given by \(B = \frac{\mu_0 I}{4\pi d} (\sin\theta_1 + \sin\theta_2)\). For a square of edge length 'a', the distance from the center to each side is \(d = a/2\). The angles \(\theta_1\) and \(\theta_2\) for each segment are \(45^\circ\), so \(\sin\theta_1 = \sin\theta_2 = \frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\).
B_{segment} = \frac{\mu_0 I}{4\pi (a/2)} \left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}} + \frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\right) = \frac{\mu_0 I}{2\pi a} \frac{2}{\sqrt{2}} = \frac{\sqrt{2}\mu_0 I}{2\pi a}
Using the right-hand rule:
• For segments AB and BC (current \(i_1 = 2I/3\)), the magnetic field at the center is directed into the page (negative \(\hat{k}\) direction).
• For segments CD and DA (current \(i_2 = I/3\)), the magnetic field at the center is directed out of the page (positive \(\hat{k}\) direction).
\vec{B} = \vec{B}_{AB} + \vec{B}_{BC} + \vec{B}_{CD} + \vec{B}_{DA}
\vec{B}_{AB} = -\frac{\sqrt{2}\mu_0 (2I/3)}{2\pi a} \hat{k}
\vec{B}_{BC} = -\frac{\sqrt{2}\mu_0 (2I/3)}{2\pi a} \hat{k}
\vec{B}_{CD} = +\frac{\sqrt{2}\mu_0 (I/3)}{2\pi a} \hat{k}
\vec{B}_{DA} = +\frac{\sqrt{2}\mu_0 (I/3)}{2\pi a} \hat{k}

### Step 3: Sum the magnetic fields

\vec{B} = \left[ -\frac{\sqrt{2}\mu_0 (2I/3)}{2\pi a} - \frac{\sqrt{2}\mu_0 (2I/3)}{2\pi a} + \frac{\sqrt{2}\mu_0 (I/3)}{2\pi a} + \frac{\sqrt{2}\mu_0 (I/3)}{2\pi a} \right] \hat{k}
\vec{B} = \left[ -2 \times \frac{\sqrt{2}\mu_0 (2I/3)}{2\pi a} + 2 \times \frac{\sqrt{2}\mu_0 (I/3)}{2\pi a} \right] \hat{k}
\vec{B} = \left[ -\frac{2\sqrt{2}\mu_0 I}{3\pi a} + \frac{\sqrt{2}\mu_0 I}{3\pi a} \right] \hat{k}
\vec{B} = \left[ -\frac{\sqrt{2}\mu_0 I}{3\pi a} \right] \hat{k}
The magnitude of the resultant magnetic field at the center of the square loop is \(\frac{\sqrt{2}\mu_0 I}{3\pi a}\).
The magnitude of the resultant magnetic field at the centre of the square loop is \(\frac{\sqrt{2}\mu_0 I}{3\pi a}\).

