Given \(f(x) = x - 1\)
First, find \(f(f(x))\):
f(f(x)) = f(x) - 1 = (x - 1) - 1 = x - 2
Next, find \(g(f(f(x)))\) using \(g(x) = e^x\):
g(f(f(x))) = e^{x-2}
Substitute this into the given differential equation:
